-- title:
--   Depth-first search program, ordered forest, and timestamp specifications
-- statement:
--   The concrete recursive depth-first search accepts either an arbitrary vertex-root permutation or constructs identity order. The generated Call interfaces describe these executions. A fresh result object contains six distinct fresh arrays for colors, parents, discovery and finish times, increasing finish order, and predecessor-tree labels. The mathematical forest contract includes edge-valid parents, distinct events in 1,…,2n, nested or disjoint intervals, ancestor equivalence, induced-white-path reachability, root-order priority, a finish-order permutation, and dense nonempty tree labels. These labels describe DFS trees, not strongly connected components. This bundle contains definitions and generated interfaces, with no DFS correctness or runtime proof.
-- source:
--   CLRS, Introduction to Algorithms, fourth edition (MIT Press, 2022), Chapter 20, §20.3. https://mitpress.mit.edu/9780262046305/introduction-to-algorithms/ ; new arrays-of-arrays implementation compiled with Algo2Lean v0.1.4, https://www.algo2lean.com/versions/v0.1.4/ . Source filenames and full code are in the mission description.

